-- The auction library (auction-cat Auction/*.lean, slice A3) as
-- definitions over Fin, Flag and matOfFn (D63-D69). The Makefile joins this
-- file after finstoch.lang, so each name here is a core name too (rule R4).
-- A strategy is a map Fin n -> Fin n. In a joint bid or an outcome of
-- Fin (natMul x y), the first bidder is the low digit. Ties go to the lowest
-- bidder index. The Lean lets are helper parameters: an At helper takes the
-- bids, a Win helper also takes the win flags (D74).
-- Strategies: truthful (Lean id, Examples.lean:202), halfShading (Bidder.lean:114).
def truthful : (n : Nat) -> (v : Fin n) -> Fin n :=
  fun (n : Nat) (v : Fin n) => v
def halfShading : (n : Nat) -> (v : Fin n) -> Fin n :=
  fun (n : Nat) (v : Fin n) => finSub v (natSub (finVal v) (natDiv (finVal v) 2))
-- 2-bidder utilities (SecondPrice.lean, FirstPrice.lean, ReserveTruth.lean,
